From f9a42bbbb8d2a349df1a4b5793570caa311f4bdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:42:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(chem108): keep the trial's account answer with the
 session that asked

The public trial page asked MCC.user() once, latched verified = true on
whatever came back and never looked again. A lookup that answered after
sign-out, or after another account took the session, left "Welcome back /
Play Chemistry" on an expired guest trial for as long as the tab lived
(deep audit 2026-11-09, finding W4).

An account answer now counts only for the account whose session asked,
and only while that session is stored:

- every lookup is bound to the stored session's account and a generation.
  Sign-out, another account, cleared storage and a frozen page move the
  generation, so an answer still in flight arrives late and is dropped
- "verified" is read against storage at every decision instead of being
  remembered. mcc:auth-changed, session storage events, a return to the
  tab, a page restored from the back/forward cache and the 30 s timer all
  re-check it; the timer no longer stands down once an account answered
- a round only the account allowed closes at sign-out; a round the trial
  still covers goes on and stops claiming an account
- a refreshed token for the same account is not a sign-out (canonical auth
  refreshes while it fetches the user); a token that names no account is
  only ever equal to itself
- a failed lookup still grants nothing and still costs a guest nothing,
  and is asked again on the next return to the tab

scripts/test/chem108-trial-account.test.mjs drives the page against the
real js/mcc-auth.js over a hand-answered fetch: 18 of its 23 cases fail on
the previous module, 5 are controls.

